<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Load bearing for the signed build, and for nothing else.

      Under the hardened runtime, which notarization requires, an app may
      not send Apple events to another app without this. SwarmBar sends
      them constantly: reading a terminal's screen to find a selector,
      pressing the option that matches, pasting an inline reply, and
      focusing the tab a session runs in. Every one of those is an Apple
      event to iTerm2.

      Without it the signed build would still launch, still show every
      session, and silently fail at Approve, Deny, Reply and Open in
      Terminal, while the unsigned development build kept working
      perfectly. That is why this is here before the first release rather
      than after the first bug report.

      Nothing else is claimed. The app is deliberately unsandboxed (it
      reads other tools' state directories), and no other hardened runtime
      exception is needed: spawning pgrep, lsof and osascript is allowed
      without one.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
